  title: Imigongo
  subtitle: traditional Rwandan pattern
  story: A traditional Rwandan art form characterized by its bold, geometric patterns,
    sharp zigzags, spirals, and relief textures. Originating in the 18th century
    within the ancient Gisaka Kingdom. It was historically used to decorate the walls
    of royal huts.
